herefore we think it's  of utmost importance to keep the schools  open and  never close them again  of course  schools are set to be open at least in  the northern hemisphere now but we're  approaching autumn in winter here and  that usually means more viral infections  interesting enough  pediatricians already observe a  surprising surge of other viral  infections like the respiratory  syncytial virus which normally occurs  mostly in winter  what does that tell us about the kids  immunocompetence has has it been  weakened severely by those months of  isolation  well as a matter of fact the minor  competence hasn't changed at all it's  just that they haven't been exposed to  for instance the  rs virus  last winter and therefore they are not  immune against it  and now they are getting their immune  system gets confronted with those viral  agents for instance  and that causes a much larger population  of children to be infected and also be  admitted into the hospital awards  you even i mean there are kids with  respiratory infections in your words as  well and it's not kobe 19 how serious is  it  that's absolutely right at the very  moment it's a paradoxical situation if  you wish  we have about  well 20 to 30  patients  on the wards with  respiratory infections other than covet  and we haven't had any covet infections  at least in our hospital within the last  two to three weeks  and that even though in most industrial  countries  schools are open again but what does  that mean for kids aged 10 to 14 right  now they're in the highest coronavirus  incidence group will they all be  infected eventually  well  we we think as a matter of fact that  eventually everybody will be infected  within the next couple of years  however  the the situation for the children is  not as bad as for adults if they get  infected they have a milder cause as we  just pointed out on the other hand we  don't want to have them all infected at  the same time first of all some children  have a 